    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d727">

                <pb facs="1208" n="1194" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1194"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115a/3343: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Acting American Representative to the French Committee of National
                        Liberation at Algiers</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Chapin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-31">January 31,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>331. Your despatch 16, December 4, and telegram 122, January 12.<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d727-f1"/>
                </p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>A basic principle of Department’s instruction 1202 February 14, 1942, to
                        Legation Bern<anchor n="9" xml:id="d727-f2"/> is to expedite extension of
                        financial assistance by the designation of a central office in the field: <list>
                            <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                            <item>to review applications granted on the spot (those covered by
                                paragraph 10 of 1202); and</item>
                            <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)</label>
                            <item>to render decisions on all other applications (paragraph 11 of
                                1202).</item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                    <label/>
                    <item>Such centralization also assures a uniform and consistent application of
                        1202 within a given area.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Department wishes to designate one such Central Office in each liberated
                        country. Central Office will accept and decide upon all applications
                        submitted by American nationals within its immediate jurisdiction. It will
                        also review or render decision upon applications submitted to other offices
                        in the same country, all of which are to be forwarded to the Central Office.
                        Central Office will endorse all applications to show, in case of review, its
                        concurrence in or reversal of decision taken by initiating office and, in
                        other cases, its decision. Central Office will then forward endorsed
                        applications to Department as provided by paragraph 2 of Department’s 2188,
                        November 18.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d727-f3"/>
                    </item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Qualified American nationals on lists received from Swiss representatives
                        pursuant to paragraph 4 (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) of memorandum of
                        December 15 transmitted with Department’s instruction to Murphy<anchor
                            n="11" xml:id="d727-f4"/> of December 27<anchor n="12" xml:id="d727-f5"
                        /> may be considered in same category as applicants covered by paragraph 10
                        of 1202.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>If you believe that Palermo,<anchor n="13" xml:id="d727-f6"/> for the time
                        being, is best situated to serve as Central Office for liberated Italy, you
                        are hereby authorized so to designate it and to instruct Palermo in
                        foregoing sense.</item>
                    <label>5.</label>
                    <item>At the appropriate time, there should be similarly designated a Central
                        Office for liberated France, financial assistance having already <pb
                            facs="1209" n="1195" xml:id="pg1195"/> been authorized in Tunisia
                        (Department’s 11, September 4, to Tunis<anchor n="14" xml:id="d727-f7"/>)
                        and Corsica (Department’s 83, December 7, to you<anchor n="15"
                            xml:id="d727-f8"/>). Your recommendations in that respect are requested.
                        If you consider it desirable, you may authorize Tunis to continue to
                        function independently.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
